  "description": "Cascadia: The Classic Self-Contained Touring Bike with Modern Features\nThe Cascadia is the ultimate touring bike for those who crave the perfect balance of classic design and modern performance. Built to handle heavy loads with ease, this bike excels at long-distance tours with a smooth ride and exceptional stability. If we hadn’t already created the Americano for epic transcontinental expeditions, we’d call the Cascadia the world’s best road touring bike.\nKey Features:\n\nOptimized for 700c Wheels: Compatible with 28mm–38mm tires for a fast, comfortable ride on paved and mixed-terrain roads.\n\nColumbus Tubing: Exclusive lightweight and durable steel construction, providing the perfect balance of strength and comfort.\n\nThru-Axles for Enhanced Stability: 142x12mm rear and 100x12mm front thru-axles ensure precise handling, even under heavy loads.\n\nShimano Ultegra 2x11-Speed Gearing: Wide-range gearing for smooth, reliable shifting over varying terrain.\n\nSteel Uni-Crown Touring Fork: Designed for stability and comfort on long tours, whether you're on smooth pavement or rougher roads.\n\nCo-Motion Touring Geometry: Proven geometry for a stable, comfortable ride during long-distance trips.\n\nRack, Fender, and Bottle Mounts: Equipped to carry all your gear, with three bottle mounts for hydration on the go.\n\nMechanical Disc Brakes and Hand-Built Wheels: Reliable stopping power and rugged wheels for all your touring needs.\n\nThe Cascadia is built for serious touring, offering the perfect mix of classic durability and modern innovation. Whether you’re embarking on a weekend getaway or a long-haul adventure, this bike is ready to take you the distance.\n\nClick here to get your Co-Motion Cascadia order started!",
